      "content": "To improve your model's granularity, consider integrating variables like population density, edema of schools, and the presence of commercial centers, which often drive localized claim patterns. Exposures from municipal infrastructure conditions, such as road quality or setback distances, and even micro-climate factors like unique shade cover can also significantly impact property damage frequency. Additionally, leveraging historical micro-zoning data and specific crime metrics at the street level rather than the broader neighborhood zone may help capture the unexplained variance currently affecting your results.",
